  ["decision: club-shinshi's V1 crypto monetization is receive-only (buyer -> gftd,
    one-directional, gftd as ordinary merchant) -- NOT creator payout. Creator payout
    (buyer -> gftd -> creator) is explicitly deferred to a future ADR/task"
   "reason for the narrowing: a code-level check of the existing etzhayyim ERC-4337
    actor infra (EtzhayyimActorRegistry.sol, EtzhayyimPaymaster.sol) found it unsafe to
    build creator payout on yet -- registry activate() has no access control (DID
    front-running/hijack), paymaster allowlist doesn't enforce function selector or
    recipient (contradicts its own README policy), and the deployed self-custody wallet
    pair lives on etzhayyim's private single-sealer chain, not the public Base L2 the
    payments policy targets. Paymaster itself is undeployed/unaudited stub v0.0.0"
   "implementation: 0008_crypto_pay.sql (pay_run ledger) + shinshi.worker.payments
    (buyer-facing quote/claim/status) + shinshi.worker.d1-gateway ops
    (list_pending_pay_runs, confirm_pay_run) + bb.edn/tools/verify-payments.clj, all
    reusing kotoba-lang/treasury (treasury.core) directly -- club-shinshi's OWN separate
    treasury address, never local-murakumo's (ADR-2607052100 commingling finding applies
    to receive-only rails too)"
   "build verified in an isolated west worktree: shadow-cljs worker build succeeds,
    npm test 24/24 tests (1078 assertions) pass, babashka verifier safely no-ops with
    secrets unset. SHINSHI_TREASURY_ADDR is unset by default -- no real wallet
    provisioned, no mainnet transaction, no legal/compliance certification in this pass"]
